# Citation metadata for THIS CODE REPOSITORY (Apache-2.0). The published
# dataset itself (CC BY 4.0) is a separate archive with its own citation -
# see docs/DESIGN.md §10 for the license split and the data descriptor
# article for the dataset DOI once it exists.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: focuswatch-dataset
abstract: >-
  Converts four heterogeneous wrist/head-IMU, pen and observer-annotation
  capture pipelines into one canonical, physically validated Parquet dataset
  for a journal data descriptor.
# `authors` is mandatory in CFF 1.2.0 - without it GitHub's citation widget and
# cffconvert both reject the file. Listed here is authorship of THIS CODE.
# Co-authorship of the DATASET across the partner cohorts is a separate and
# still-open question (see docs/DESIGN.md §3); settle it before the archive is
# minted rather than inheriting this list.
authors:
  - family-names: Samel
    given-names: Noah
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/CH-GE-Focus-Watch/focuswatch-dataset
version: 0.1.0
# PLACEHOLDER - not a real DOI. Zenodo mints one automatically on the first
# tagged GitHub release once the Zenodo-GitHub integration (DESIGN §10) is
# enabled; replace this whole `doi` line at that point, do not invent a value
# before then.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.PLACEHOLDER
